    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0668" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg618"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 226.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose, with
                    translation, an extract from El Liberal of the 22d instant, indicating the
                    course to be taken by the custom-house authorities of Cuba and Porto Rico as to
                    imposition of tariff dues upon merchandise from the United States the moment
                    that the new tariff bill takes effect.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>




